 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Rules of case and order with two complements",
     "texto": [
      "1. **Case assignment**: The recipient or beneficiary goes in the Dative (**wem?**); the transferred object goes in the Accusative (**was?**): **Die Kollegin erklärt den Mitarbeitern (Dativ) die Aufgabe (Akkusativ)**.",
      "2. **Order with two nouns**: The dative comes before the accusative: **Ich gebe dem Kunden (Dat) den Vertrag (Akk)**.",
      "3. **Order with a pronoun and a noun**: The pronoun always goes first, regardless of case: **Ich gebe ihm (pronoun Dat) den Vertrag (noun Akk)**; **Ich gebe ihn (pronoun Akk) dem Kunden (noun Dat)**.",
      "4. **Order with two pronouns**: The accusative always comes before the dative: **Ich gebe ihn (Akk) ihm (Dat)**; **Er erklärt es (Akk) mir (Dat)**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Combination",
     "columnas": [
